# Nurturing Pixie: "a ... permanent you control" is control, not ownership, and it goes "to its owner's hand" (CR 400.3).
# Bot2 plays Mox Jet on turn 2; on turn 3 Bot1 casts Dack Fayden (Mox Sapphire, Mox Ruby, Plains) and takes the Mox
# with his -2, then casts the Pixie, which returns that Mox to Bot2's hand. It was returned, so the Pixie is 2/2.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Plains
Plains
Dack Fayden
Nurturing Pixie
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Jet
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains#1.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dack Fayden.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
Bot1.Battlefield.Dack Fayden.Activate(Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet; Ability: Gain control)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Nurturing Pixie.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains#2.Activate
Bot1.Target(Mox Jet)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass

